    "q-276692": {
      "dom_id": "step-q276692",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "What is the range of the function $f(x)=-\\frac{9}{2x+9}+5\\,?$\n\nThe range is\n$f(x)\\in (${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$)\\cup (${{field-3}}$,\\infty ).$",
      "worked_solution": "A transformed reciprocal function of the form\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{a}{bx+c}+d\n$$\n\nhas the horizontal asymptote $y=d,$ and therefore, its range is\n\n$$\nf(x)\\in (-\\infty ,d)\\cup (d,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $d=5.$ Therefore, the horizontal asymptote is $y=5,$ and the range of the function is\n\n$$\nf(x)\\in (-\\infty ,5)\\cup (5,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nThe graph $y=f(x)$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14248368/assets/0da9b33dde51888d770d9e095d74b628698d870727a53f252948d99644c7bc3d.png)",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
