    "q-106747": {
      "dom_id": "step-q106747",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "What is the range of $f(x)=\\frac{5}{4-x}-3?$",
      "worked_solution": "A transformed reciprocal function of the form\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{a}{bx+c}+d\n$$\n\nhas the horizontal asymptote $y=d,$ and therefore, its range is\n\n$$\nf(x)\\in (-\\infty ,d)\\cup (d,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $d=-3.$ Therefore, the horizontal asymptote is $y=-3,$ and the range of the function is\n\n$$\nf(x)\\in (-\\infty ,-3)\\cup (-3,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nThe graph $y=f(x)$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14248368/assets/b1b6683bab3caf6fc2350c14382266483c848e6b0490d4d1b7cf6c5f5d2ad273.png)",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
